.TH MCR 1 "August 2026" "rusty-midnight-commander" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcr \- dual-pane terminal file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcr
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcr
is the binary of rusty-midnight-commander, an Apache-2.0 clean-room
Rust file manager aiming for GNU Midnight Commander
.RI ( mc )
user-visible behavior.
.PP
With no options it opens a dual-pane listing of the current directory:
menu bar (F9), two directory panels, mini-status, hint line, shell
command line, and an F1\-F10 label bar.
.PP
This page describes the
.B mcr
command line only. It is original Apache-2.0 text summarizing shipped
behavior. It is not a copy of the GNU
.BR mc (1)
manual.
.SH OPTIONS
Unknown flags are ignored so a later
.BR \-\-edit ,
.BR \-\-view ,
or
.B \-\-diff
is still honored.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-nomouse
Do not capture the mouse for this run.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-nosubshell
Do not attach a PTY subshell. Last of
.B \-U
/
.B \-u
wins.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-subshell
Enable the PTY subshell (Ctrl-O). Last of
.B \-U
/
.B \-u
wins.
.TP
.BR \-S " " \fIname\fR ", " \-\-skin \fR[\fB=\fIname\fR]
Skin name for this process (overrides
.B MC_SKIN
and the user ini). A missing name keeps the requested label and falls
back to the default palette.
.TP
.BR \-v " " \fIfile\fR ", " \-\-view \fR[\fB=\fIfile\fR]
Start the internal viewer on
.IR file .
See
.BR mcr-view (1).
.TP
.BR \-e " [" \fIfile\fR "...]", " " \-\-edit \fR[\fB=\fIfile\fR]
Start the internal editor. With no files, one untitled buffer is
opened. See
.BR mcr-edit (1).
.TP
.B \-\-diff \fIfile1 file2\fR
Start the internal side-by-side diff viewer. See
.BR mcr-diff (1).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH ARCHIVES
Enter on a supported archive browses it as a directory;
.B ..
leaves it. Copy from inside an archive to a local panel extracts
(copy-out). Creating, deleting, renaming, or copying
.I into
an archive is refused (read-only file system). FTP
.RB ( ftp://
/ \fB/#ftp:\fR), SFTP
.RB ( sftp://
/ \fB/#sftp:\fR), and FISH
.RB ( sh://
/ \fB/#sh:\fR) panels support copy-in, mkdir, rename, and delete when
the server allows.
.PP
Shipped browse + copy-out backends: tar, tar.gz/tgz, zip, cpio
(and cpio.gz), ar, rpm, deb, iso, rar, 7z, lha/lzh.
Zoo archives are not implemented.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mc/ini
User configuration. Loaded after compiled-in defaults and the first
existing system file. Options \-> Save setup writes this file (and
creates
.I ~/.config/mc/
as needed). Quit does the same when Options \-> Panels \-> Auto save
setup is on. Unknown keys and sections are preserved.
.I $MC_PROFILE_ROOT
(absolute) relocates the profile; otherwise
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mc
or
.IR ~/.config/mc .
.I $MCR_CONFIG_DIR
overrides the setup directory for tests.
.TP
.I /etc/mc/mc.ini
System-wide setup (used if present).
.TP
.I /usr/share/mc/mc.ini
System-wide setup used when
.I /etc/mc/mc.ini
is missing. When
.B MC_DATADIR
is set, this path is
.IR $MC_DATADIR/mc.ini
instead. The user file overlays the system file.
.TP
.I data/help/
Built-in hypertext help shown with F1 (also embedded in the binary).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcr-edit (1),
.BR mcr-view (1),
.BR mcr-diff (1)
.PP
F1 inside
.B mcr
opens the hypertext help. GNU Midnight Commander manuals
.BR mc (1),
.BR mcedit (1),
.BR mcview (1),
and
.BR mcdiff (1)
document the public behavior this project tracks; they are separate
GPL works and are not shipped here.
.SH INSTALLING THIS MANUAL
From a source checkout:
.PP
.nf
man \-l docs/man/mcr.1
sudo install \-D \-m 644 docs/man/mcr.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/mcr.1
sudo install \-D \-m 644 docs/man/mcr\-edit.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/mcr\-edit.1
sudo install \-D \-m 644 docs/man/mcr\-view.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/mcr\-view.1
sudo install \-D \-m 644 docs/man/mcr\-diff.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/mcr\-diff.1
.fi
